                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Words cannot express how delightful it was to play through this again. this is a review from both past me, who would sit on the computer in 15, and then in 30 minute rounds with my siblings as we would gather around the computer, pooling our computer time into one block so we could spend and hour and a half, and then two hours playing games together. we would play Word Rescue, Math Rescue, and other games. some faded as the years went and some stuck around. all the triumphs, defeats, discussions, arguments, fights, and learning opportunities we had. this game had me feeling nostalgia but also allowed me to contemplate how it was, how it is, and how one day it will become.\n\nI blitzed through this, being much, much older than I was back then. I died a couple of times to misstimed jumps around slime pools, got hit by a dropping gruzzle, and failed to solve two words because I wanted to see if you got the bonus points for completing them in any order or only sequentially. after finishing the game I learnt that there was two other difficulty levels, the game was set on Easy (4-7 year olds). I'm wondering if higher levels have more complex words and more gruzzles and will explore that at my liesure. \n\nif you have young children, let them play this. better yet, stay beside them and have fun together. if they have siblings maybe see if you can get them to play along with each other for a bit, or a lot. it's word association, spelling, fine-motor control, decision making, problem solving, and memory recall all working together.\n\nand when they go to bed, come back and beat the game for yourself.",
